<article class="env-definition" id="069F">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/069F">Definition <span data-tag="069F">37.62.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Let $x \in X$. We say that $f$ is <em>Koszul at $x$</em> if $f$ is of finite type at $x$ and there exists an open neighbourhood and a factorization of $f|_ U$ as $\pi \circ i$ where $i : U \to P$ is a Koszul-regular immersion and $\pi : P \to S$ is smooth. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
We say $f$ is a <em>Koszul morphism</em>, or that $f$ is a <em>local complete intersection morphism</em> if $f$ is Koszul at every point. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>